      "content": "i get that the brain likes patterns, but it's more than just seeing things that aren't there. the timing is what's tripping me out. it's happening right when certain social shifts are being pushed by big platforms. if you look at how these things are engineered to trigger specific emotional responses, couldn't they be used as a way to gauge how much people will just go along with whatever is being fed to them? like, a way to test compliance through basically \"saturating\" the environment? i'm trying to figure out if there's actually a methodology behind it or if i'm just overthinking things.",
